 "kicker": "Contention · decode_syndrome",
 "summary": "Each logical qubit produces a decoding job every few syndrome rounds. If the decoder is slower than the rounds, jobs queue and the backlog grows without bound. How many RISC-Q decoder cores keep up, against a count that reserves a decoder for the worst case of every decode.",
 "method": [
  "Jobs arrive at the round period (1.1 µs for superconducting, 4.45 ms for neutral atoms, 2 ms for ions); each lasts a decode time drawn from the compiled decoder's measured decodes for that distance and window; QuantumOS's runtime simulator queues them on c cores. A stream is stable when the worst wait per window does not grow along it. The static count reserves the worst decode for every job."
